# Tiny copy / doer + adversary

Keep in sync with Place et Marque `workflows/tiny-copy-edit.md` and Project `scripts/cv-summary-patch.sh` / `tiny-copy-verify.sh`.

## When this path applies

All of: ≤ ~2 sentences; known file (`--file`); exact unique old string; no layout/CSS/design judgment.

Otherwise use a normal doer agent.

## Protocol (exact drop-ins)

- **same_vm-local** default: warm coordinator/peer runs patch + verify on this host.
- **Do not** `CreateAgent` a new doer/adversary for unambiguous drop-ins — boot/hops dominate the budget.
- Paste-only: `--new` is user text verbatim (JSX-escape if the file uses `&apos;`). Doer and adversary must not rewrite.
- Fail-closed verify required (lint evidence + exact diff + EOL). Re-read/`rg`-only is not verify.
- Preserve EOL (CRLF stays CRLF). LF rewrite of a CRLF file → adversary REJECT.
- Portfolio git: commit only on `feature/<user>/development/<slug>`; ff-merge to `development`; never commit on `development`/`master`.
- Budget: ≤ **30s** wall user message → pushed SHA + adversary ACCEPT.

## Do not

- `./bin/agent-cli orient`, repo tour, or worktree theater for this class of edit.
- Spawn more agents to “finish” after the wall is blown — record why instead.
